{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019nP2zj39f4BVBLhzHmXS6e","type":"tool_result","content":"/bin/bash: /etc/bash.bashrc: Permission denied\n/ux/set/bin/metais\nInvoice — invoice 1.0.0\nRenders one HTML invoice, with a line for each item and their total, from a JSON object a program supplies.\nMETAIS 1.0, packed, sha256:1670c16355816f0d240a181e12dddd54c32e6ec35db48e0e5cf94a6be26d4057\n\nGuide\nThis package renders invoice.html, an HTML page that prints one invoice:\nits number and the date it was issued, the seller and the buyer, a table\nof the items invoiced with each line's amount, the total, and optional\nnotes. The page carries class names and no style of its own.\n\nIt is written for a program, not a person. A billing job reads the\ninvoice from wherever it is kept, writes it as invoice.json in a data\ndirectory, and runs two commands:\n\n    metais validate invoice --data data\n    metais render invoice --data data --out out\n\nvalidate reports every value that does not fit the\n[invoice schema](inputs/invoice.schema.json), and render writes\nout/invoice.html. Every value is HTML-escaped, so a name, an address, a\ndescription or a note may hold any text.\n\nEach line's amount is its quantity times its unit price, and the total is\nthe sum of the amounts; the program supplies neither. Every amount is in\nthe invoice's one currency, given as its three-letter ISO 4217 code.\nLeave notes out when there is nothing to add.\n\nInputs\n  invoice — Invoice (required; invoice.json)\n    One invoice, as the billing program that issues it holds it.\n\nOutputs\n  invoice.html ← template invoice.html.liquid\n\nReferences\n  1 entry, 771 B\n  references/sources.md (771 B) — Sources and their terms\n\nExamples\n  basic: invoice (with expected outputs)\n  escaping: invoice (with expected outputs)\n\nNext:\n  metais schema <package> invoice  — Prints the schema the input invoice is validated against.\n  metais ls <package> examples/basic/ -r  — Lists the first example's inputs and expected outputs.\n  metais grep <package> <pattern> references/  — Searches the package's references.\n  metais validate <package> --data <dir>  — Validates the inputs you gathered in a data directory.\n  metais render <package> --data <dir> --out <dir>  — Renders the outputs from the validated inputs into a new directory.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4dde7ed6-a656-48ee-979d-1bd9908210ab","uuid":"e79c47c1-77f0-41aa-b461-32fea7ca7d70","timestamp":"2026-10-21T14:05:09.176Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/bin/bash: /etc/bash.bashrc: Permission denied\n/ux/set/bin/metais\nInvoice — invoice 1.0.0\nRenders one HTML invoice, with a line for each item and their total, from a JSON object a program supplies.\nMETAIS 1.0, packed, sha256:1670c16355816f0d240a181e12dddd54c32e6ec35db48e0e5cf94a6be26d4057\n\nGuide\nThis package renders invoice.html, an HTML page that prints one invoice:\nits number and the date it was issued, the seller and the buyer, a table\nof the items invoiced with each line's amount, the total, and optional\nnotes. The page carries class names and no style of its own.\n\nIt is written for a program, not a person. A billing job reads the\ninvoice from wherever it is kept, writes it as invoice.json in a data\ndirectory, and runs two commands:\n\n    metais validate invoice --data data\n    metais render invoice --data data --out out\n\nvalidate reports every value that does not fit the\n[invoice schema](inputs/invoice.schema.json), and render writes\nout/invoice.html. Every value is HTML-escaped, so a name, an address, a\ndescription or a note may hold any text.\n\nEach line's amount is its quantity times its unit price, and the total is\nthe sum of the amounts; the program supplies neither. Every amount is in\nthe invoice's one currency, given as its three-letter ISO 4217 code.\nLeave notes out when there is nothing to add.\n\nInputs\n  invoice — Invoice (required; invoice.json)\n    One invoice, as the billing program that issues it holds it.\n\nOutputs\n  invoice.html ← template invoice.html.liquid\n\nReferences\n  1 entry, 771 B\n  references/sources.md (771 B) — Sources and their terms\n\nExamples\n  basic: invoice (with expected outputs)\n  escaping: invoice (with expected outputs)\n\nNext:\n  metais schema <package> invoice  — Prints the schema the input invoice is validated against.\n  metais ls <package> examples/basic/ -r  — Lists the first example's inputs and expected outputs.\n  metais grep <package> <pattern> references/  — Searches the package's references.\n  metais validate <package> --data <dir>  — Validates the inputs you gathered in a data directory.\n  metais render <package> --data <dir> --out <dir>  — Renders the outputs from the validated inputs into a new directory.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019nP2zj39f4BVBLhzHmXS6e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
